   "source": [
    "#Estimo los coeficientes por regresión en el conjunto de train\n",
    "data = pd.concat([x_train, x_train.shift(1), x_train.shift(2)], axis=1).dropna()\n",
    "data.columns = [\"x\", \"xL1\", \"xL2\"]\n",
    "#Ajusto\n",
    "fit = ols(\"x ~ 0+xL1+xL2\", data=data).fit()\n",
    "residuo=fit.resid\n",
    "fit.summary() #el coef. hallado es la correlación de xt y xt-1, es decir acf(1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "Pero también podemos usar las funciones incorporadas en `statsmodels`. En particular, los modelos autorregresivos son parte de la clase general de modelos ARIMA que veremos más adelante, por lo que usamos la función de ajuste de los mismos."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "fragment"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<table class=\"simpletable\">\n",
       "<caption>SARIMAX Results</caption>\n",
       "<tr>\n",
       "  <th>Dep. Variable:</th>           <td>y</td>        <th>  No. Observations:  </th>    <td>500</td>  \n",
       "</tr>\n",
       "<tr>\n",
       "  <th>Model:</th>            <td>ARIMA(2, 0, 0)</td>  <th>  Log Likelihood     </th> <td>-704.752</td>\n",
       "</tr>\n",
       "<tr>\n",
       "  <th>Date:</th>            <td>Mon, 25 May 2026</td> <th>  AIC                </th> <td>1415.505</td>\n",
       "</tr>\n",
       "<tr>\n",
       "  <th>Time:</th>                <td>17:02:46</td>     <th>  BIC                </th> <td>1428.148</td>\n",
       "</tr>\n",
       "<tr>\n",
       "  <th>Sample:</th>                  <td>0</td>        <th>  HQIC               </th> <td>1420.466</td>\n",
       "</tr>\n",
