              "  <th>Kurtosis:</th>      <td> 3.137</td> <th>  Cond. No.          </th> <td>    1.00</td>\n",
              "</tr>\n",
              "</table><br/><br/>Notes:<br/>[1] R² is computed without centering (uncentered) since the model does not contain a constant.<br/>[2] Standard Errors assume that the covariance matrix of the errors is correctly specified."
            ],
            "text/latex": "\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tabular}{lclc}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Dep. Variable:}    &       xL2        & \\textbf{  R-squared (uncentered):}      &     0.294   \\\\\n\\textbf{Model:}            &       OLS        & \\textbf{  Adj. R-squared (uncentered):} &     0.292   \\\\\n\\textbf{Method:}           &  Least Squares   & \\textbf{  F-statistic:       }          &     206.8   \\\\\n\\textbf{Date:}             & Mon, 11 May 2026 & \\textbf{  Prob (F-statistic):}          &  1.84e-39   \\\\\n\\textbf{Time:}             &     22:38:22     & \\textbf{  Log-Likelihood:    }          &   -1131.4   \\\\\n\\textbf{No. Observations:} &         498      & \\textbf{  AIC:               }          &     2265.   \\\\\n\\textbf{Df Residuals:}     &         497      & \\textbf{  BIC:               }          &     2269.   \\\\\n\\textbf{Df Model:}         &           1      & \\textbf{                     }          &             \\\\\n\\textbf{Covariance Type:}  &    nonrobust     & \\textbf{                     }          &             \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\begin{tabular}{lcccccc}\n             & \\textbf{coef} & \\textbf{std err} & \\textbf{t} & \\textbf{P$> |$t$|$} & \\textbf{[0.025} & \\textbf{0.975]}  \\\\\n\\midrule\n\\textbf{xL1} &       0.5421  &        0.038     &    14.382  &         0.000        &        0.468    &        0.616     \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\begin{tabular}{lclc}\n\\textbf{Omnibus:}       &  1.275 & \\textbf{  Durbin-Watson:     } &    1.038  \\\\\n\\textbf{Prob(Omnibus):} &  0.529 & \\textbf{  Jarque-Bera (JB):  } &    1.075  \\\\\n\\textbf{Skew:}          &  0.091 & \\textbf{  Prob(JB):          } &    0.584  \\\\\n\\textbf{Kurtosis:}      &  3.137 & \\textbf{  Cond. No.          } &     1.00  \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n%\\caption{OLS Regression Results}\n\\end{center}\n\nNotes: \\newline\n [1] R² is computed without centering (uncentered) since the model does not contain a constant. \\newline\n [2] Standard Errors assume that the covariance matrix of the errors is correctly specified."
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 36
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Ajusto r2\n",
        "fit2 = ols(\"xL2 ~ 0+xL1\", data=data).fit()\n",
        "r2=fit2.resid\n",
        "fit2.summary() #el coef. hallado es la correlación de xt y xt-1, es decir acf(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 37,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ziw7mmoDcbgJ",
        "outputId": "2c7acf4d-724f-403e-8a8c-6cb1b72bdbf7",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.scatter(r1,r2);\n",
        "plt.title(f\"Correlación remanente: {np.corrcoef(r1,r2)[0,1]}\");"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IUpUNuuxcbgJ"
      },
      "source": [
        "El método anterior puede repetirse para todos los lags. Simplemente:\n",
        "\n",
        " * Ajusto $x_t$ a $x_{t-1},\\ldots,x_{t-p+1}$, obtengo $r_1$.\n",
        " * Ajusto $x_{t-p}$ a $x_{t-1},\\ldots,x_{t-p+1}$, obtengo $r_2$.\n",
        " * Calculo la correlación entre $r_1$ y $r_2$ (o bien ajusto lineal $r_2$ a $r_1$, es lo mismo). Al resultado se le llama *autocorrelación parcial* entre $x_t$ y $x_{t-p}$ (o de lag $p$).\n",
        "\n",
        " Hagamoslo un paso más ($p=3$) para ver que ya no queda información."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 38,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cdhmxbzWcbgJ"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "#Realizo el procedimiento anterior\n",
        "#Realizo el procedimiento anterior\n",
        "data = pd.concat([x, x.shift(1), x.shift(2), x.shift(3)], axis=1).dropna()\n",
        "data.columns = [\"x\", \"xL1\", \"xL2\", \"xL3\"]\n",
        "#Ajusto r1\n",
        "fit1 = ols(\"x ~ 0+xL1+xL2\", data=data).fit()\n",
        "r1=fit1.resid\n",
        "#Ajusto r2\n",
        "fit2 = ols(\"xL3 ~ 0+xL1+xL2\", data=data).fit()\n",
        "r2=fit2.resid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 39,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "w_OrGPlZcbgK",
        "outputId": "be63e807-d594-45f7-ebf4-fd7eddf96fc9",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.scatter(r1,r2);\n",
        "plt.title(f\"Correlación remanente: {np.corrcoef(r1,r2)[0,1]}\");"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "sjMEk7fbcbgK"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Función de autocorrelación parcial (PACF)\n",
        "\n",
        "* A la función así construida recursivamente se le denomina Función de Autocorrelación Parcial (PACF).\n",
        "* En el ejemplo anterior, la PACF(1) coincide con la ACF(1). La PACF(2) *NO* (es otra información).\n",
        "* En el proceso AR(2), la PACF(2) era significativa, la PACF(3) se vuelve 0.\n",
        "* En general, si un proceso es AR($p$), entonces la PACF se \"apaga\" luego de $p$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 40,
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "t_e2Kxc0cbgK",
        "outputId": "080b54a6-ae1c-457d-8bf2-8696d4038ad8",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plot_pacf(x);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "G6JFsMgbcbgK"
      },
      "source": [
        "Apliquemos la misma idea al proceso AR(1) que teníamos antes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 41,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-RAVT_S-cbgK",
        "outputId": "f4c10225-45be-412e-d240-0b15615fd753",
        "colab": {
