              "</table><br/><br/>Notes:<br/>[1] R² is computed without centering (uncentered) since the model does not contain a constant.<br/>[2] Standard Errors assume that the covariance matrix of the errors is correctly specified."
            ],
            "text/latex": "\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tabular}{lclc}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Dep. Variable:}    &        x         & \\textbf{  R-squared (uncentered):}      &     0.883   \\\\\n\\textbf{Model:}            &       OLS        & \\textbf{  Adj. R-squared (uncentered):} &     0.883   \\\\\n\\textbf{Method:}           &  Least Squares   & \\textbf{  F-statistic:       }          &     1878.   \\\\\n\\textbf{Date:}             & Mon, 11 May 2026 & \\textbf{  Prob (F-statistic):}          & 4.05e-232   \\\\\n\\textbf{Time:}             &     22:56:37     & \\textbf{  Log-Likelihood:    }          &   -716.53   \\\\\n\\textbf{No. Observations:} &         498      & \\textbf{  AIC:               }          &     1437.   \\\\\n\\textbf{Df Residuals:}     &         496      & \\textbf{  BIC:               }          &     1445.   \\\\\n\\textbf{Df Model:}         &           2      & \\textbf{                     }          &             \\\\\n\\textbf{Covariance Type:}  &    nonrobust     & \\textbf{                     }          &             \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\begin{tabular}{lcccccc}\n             & \\textbf{coef} & \\textbf{std err} & \\textbf{t} & \\textbf{P$> |$t$|$} & \\textbf{[0.025} & \\textbf{0.975]}  \\\\\n\\midrule\n\\textbf{xL1} &       1.0137  &        0.018     &    56.087  &         0.000        &        0.978    &        1.049     \\\\\n\\textbf{xL2} &      -0.9151  &        0.018     &   -50.645  &         0.000        &       -0.951    &       -0.880     \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\begin{tabular}{lclc}\n\\textbf{Omnibus:}       &  1.343 & \\textbf{  Durbin-Watson:     } &    1.960  \\\\\n\\textbf{Prob(Omnibus):} &  0.511 & \\textbf{  Jarque-Bera (JB):  } &    1.403  \\\\\n\\textbf{Skew:}          & -0.084 & \\textbf{  Prob(JB):          } &    0.496  \\\\\n\\textbf{Kurtosis:}      &  2.801 & \\textbf{  Cond. No.          } &     1.80  \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n%\\caption{OLS Regression Results}\n\\end{center}\n\nNotes: \\newline\n [1] R² is computed without centering (uncentered) since the model does not contain a constant. \\newline\n [2] Standard Errors assume that the covariance matrix of the errors is correctly specified."
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 68
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Estimo los coeficientes por regresión en el conjunto de train\n",
        "data = pd.concat([x_train, x_train.shift(1), x_train.shift(2)], axis=1).dropna()\n",
        "data.columns = [\"x\", \"xL1\", \"xL2\"]\n",
        "#Ajusto\n",
        "fit = ols(\"x ~ 0+xL1+xL2\", data=data).fit()\n",
        "residuo=fit.resid\n",
        "fit.summary() #el coef. hallado es la correlación de xt y xt-1, es decir acf(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 69,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UJ2qxrAUcbgL",
        "outputId": "6beb7039-4ac4-475a-8b70-dec01f727f3f",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Coeficientes estimados:\n",
            "phi1: 1.0137246022329214\n",
            "phi2: -0.9151315143170138\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "phi1 = fit.params[\"xL1\"]\n",
        "phi2 = fit.params[\"xL2\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Coeficientes estimados:\")\n",
        "print(f\"phi1: {phi1}\")\n",
        "print(f\"phi2: {phi2}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 70,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qJVqLbFDcbgM"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "#Construyo la prediccion recursiva\n",
        "x_test = x.iloc[n:]\n",
        "x_hat = np.empty(m)\n",
        "\n",
        "x_hat[0] = phi1 * x_train[n-1] + phi2*x_train[n-2]\n",
        "x_hat[1] = phi1 * x_hat[0] + phi2*x_train[n-1]\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(2,m):\n",
        "    x_hat[i] = phi1 * x_hat[i-1] + phi2*x_hat[i-2]\n",
        "\n",
        "#lo convierto en una serie\n",
        "x_hat = pd.Series(x_hat,index=range(n,n+m))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 71,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2EceGgS3cbgM",
        "outputId": "434faf60-4baf-4a66-d5bb-4069ef20e9e9",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.plot(x_test, label=\"Valores de test\")\n",
        "plt.plot(x_hat, label=\"Prediccion\");\n",
        "plt.legend();"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "fwxG1OEfcbgM"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Observaciones:**\n",
        "\n",
        "* La predicción solo es razonable a pocos intervalos.\n",
        "* A la larga vuelve a la media ya que promedia los valores que va obteniendo.\n",
        "* Dicho de otro modo, como la influencia de los datos hasta $n$ decae exponencialmente después de $n$, es muy difícil predecir más allá de unos pocos pasos."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "6J9RTFiGcbgM"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Predicción recursiva\n",
        "\n",
        "De todos modos, si bien no permite predecir mucho hacia el futuro, podemos ir recursivamente prediciendo el valor $x_{n+1}$ una vez que conocemos $x_{n},x_{n-1},\\ldots,x_{n-p+1}$, es decir los últimos $p$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Luego si recibimos un dato nuevo podemos actualizar la predicción."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "M97fWxOfcbgM"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Ejemplo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 50,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rJYxTbE8cbgM",
        "outputId": "10e39f63-b276-4c35-9a39-a9aa6961d0f9",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "##Simulamos un AR(2) usando la función propia de python\n",
        "x=arma_generate_sample([1,-1,.9],[1],n)\n",
        "x=pd.Series(x)\n",
        "x.plot();"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MJI3Lw1WcbgM"
      },
      "source": [
        "Supongamos que sabemos exactamente los parámetros, en este caso media $\\mu=0$, $\\phi_1=1.0$ y $\\phi_2=-0.9$.\n",
        "\n",
        " * Si solo predecimos por la media, el error MSE es el desvío estándar de la serie.\n",
        " * Si predecimos recursivamente $x_{t+1}$ por $\\hat{x}_{t+1} = \\phi_1 x_t + \\phi_2 x_{t-1}$ entonces deberíamos poder reducir el error."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 51,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-Moql11McbgM",
        "outputId": "f3cabd40-b8d5-444e-d125-cce415f14195",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "phi1 = 1.0\n",
        "phi2 = -0.9\n",
        "\n",
        "#aca va la predicción\n",
        "x_hat = np.empty(n)\n",
        "\n",
        "#los valores anteriores a t=0 los asumo 0 (la media)\n",
        "x_hat[0] = phi1*0 + phi2*0\n",
        "x_hat[1] = phi1 * x[0] + phi2*0\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(2,n):\n",
        "    x_hat[i] = phi1 * x[i-1] + phi2*x[i-2]\n",
        "\n",
        "#lo convierto en una serie\n",
        "x_hat = pd.Series(x_hat)\n",
        "\n",
        "x.plot()\n",
        "x_hat.plot();"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 52,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Q9DD7o6HcbgM",
        "outputId": "9adb4b51-126b-4630-f6e6-fe1306329164",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "##Residuo\n",
        "residuo = x-x_hat\n",
        "MSE = np.var(residuo)\n",
        "R2 = (np.var(x)-MSE)/np.var(x)\n",
        "residuo.plot()\n",
        "plt.title(f\"Residuos de la predicción: MSE = {MSE}, R2 = {R2}\");"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 53,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xm2D_pXLcbgM",
        "outputId": "2da0a214-65e6-41c1-b7d9-ffb366e38558",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plot_acf(residuo);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "3BQvy6BVcbgN"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Ejercicios\n",
        "\n",
        "### Estimación de la serie de precios de exportación del salmón noruego.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        " 1. Considere la serie `salmon` de precios de exportación de salmon noruego en dólares por kilogramo, incluida en la biblioteca `astsa` del curso.\n",
        "\n",
        "    1. Analice la autocorrelación y autocorrelación parcial de la serie.\n",
        "    2. Proponga un modelo autorregresivo de orden adecuado y ajuste el mismo. Analice los residuos obtenidos y el ajuste del modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        " 2. Se propone ahora un segundo modelo de la forma:\n",
        "$$x_t = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 t + v_t$$\n",
        "         \n",
        "    con $v_t$ autorregresivo. Realice un ajuste por modelo lineal para estimar $\\beta_0$ y $\\beta_1$.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    \n",
        " 3. Con los residuos del ajuste anterior ($v_t$), ajuste un modelo autorregresivo de orden adecuado y compare los resultados con el modelo de la primera parte."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 54,
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [],
        "id": "bJSfoziWcbgN",
        "outputId": "5fd243fe-9b29-4f41-a7cc-3ab31a198d3b",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1500x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "salmon = astsa.salmon\n",
        "salmon.plot();"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Item 1"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2Jl3ESLtV-az"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "plot_acf(salmon);"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 528
        },
        "id": "so6uoQPUUIUz",
